  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How each check works",
      "items": [
        "Mismatches: recon_account_window compares count and amount per account and window, using commit time as the window.",
        "Duplicate CDC events: the same topic, partition and offset, or the same LSN and record key, loaded more than once.",
        "Failed loads: load_batch rows with a failed status or rejected rows. Missing events: replay_event rows with no cdc_event.",
        "Inserts and updates link through last_replay_event_id in the payload. A delete only carries the previous value, so deletes match on source_table, record_pk and operation d."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Lag and late events",
      "items": [
        "Lag per hop: source_committed_at to kafka_at to landed_at to warehouse load.",
        "injected_delay_seconds makes late arrivals deliberate, so the test knows what to expect.",
        "injected_fault does the same for duplicates and failures."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Scope",
      "items": [
        "Exclude replay_run and replay_event from the Debezium table list. Airflow copies them to the audit schema in batches, so the expected changes travel separately from the pipeline being tested.",
        "The initial snapshot arrives with operation r and is not counted as a simulated change."
      ]
    }
  ]
